# Line endings for executable scripts.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# core.autocrlf is true on the dev machine and this repo had no .gitattributes, so Git
# would write CRLF into every .sh on the next checkout or clone. A shell script with CRLF
# dies at the shebang ("bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M"), which would take out all
# Claude Code hooks at once, silently: every hook fails open, so every gate turns off
# and nothing reports an error. The hooks are LF today only because tools wrote them
# directly rather than checking them out.
#
# Verify with: git ls-files --eol .claude/hooks/   (want i/lf w/lf on every row)
# Verified 2026-08-31: every tracked *.sh is already i/lf w/lf, so this pins the current
# state rather than rewriting anything. No churn.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf
# Git hooks have no extension, and bash refuses a CRLF shebang line.
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# NOT *.py, deliberately: many tracked .py files are CRLF in the worktree, and normalising them
# would rewrite them all on the next checkout for no benefit, since Python is CRLF-tolerant
# and no hook execs a .py through a shebang. If that churn is ever wanted, do it as its
# own commit with `git add --renormalize`, not as a side effect of a hook fix.

# A generated, tracked page: the generator writes LF and the file must diff clean on every machine.
docs/reference/ranged-troops.html text eol=lf
# The snapshot's project.mbproj is a byte copy of the live file (LF, UTF-8 BOM) for the same reason.
docs/reference/lotrlome-armory-snapshot/project.mbproj text eol=lf

# The /improve Workflow scripts: the Workflow tool refuses a script holding a CR ("control
# characters that would be hidden in the approval dialog"). Scoped to that folder, not *.js:
# tracked tools/*.js files are CRLF in the worktree and would churn. test_improve_workflows.py.
.claude/skills/improve/workflows/*.js text eol=lf

# The lessons files are append-only: two branches that each append a lesson at the end
# conflict, and keeping one side silently drops a lesson (merge 70c164bb3 on the 1.5.x line
# lost one that way). union keeps both sides' new lines. It cannot see a conflict, so two
# edits of the SAME existing line both survive: reread the entry after such a merge.
# Never on CHANGELOG.md (maintainer decision D18; tools/tests/test_lessons_merge_union.py).
docs/reviews/lessons/*.md merge=union
